Hello Help Me Now players! Today is a very important day for us game developers. We're here to announce a new update that will be available from the date that this announcement is posted. Help Me Now will receive an important update that reworks various aspects of the game, improving graphic, technical and game design aspects. Through this update, we implemented several improvements in graphics and ambiance, adding more particles, remodeling objects and optimizing much more. Below we will provide a list of all the improvements and changes that have been made in the game.

[olist]
[*] The graphics were remade and rethought (more realistic reflections, enhanced lighting, recalculated shadows, balanced colors, improved effects);
[*] 	The frame rate of the game is extremely high and stable;
[*] 	Well-crafted optimization;
[*] 	Recreated environments (Addition of advanced particles, remodeled models, redone textures);
[*] 	We redid the AI (Artificial Intelligence) of the enemies;
[*] 	Fixed technical issues such as bugs, glitches, crashes, and inconsistencies.
[/olist]

These were the improvements and changes made to the game. We are very happy with the result! We are trying very hard to improve your experience more and more. If you are having problems during your game please let us know by our official support email.

Best regards, Light Station Developer team.

Hello Help Me Now players! I'm here to let you know that the game has undergone a significant update in its gameplay! Below are the improvements and changes in terms of gameplay:

[list]
[*] Improved RUD;
[*] Extra Polishing;
[*] Bug fixes;
[*] The player will not need to take the tutorial to understand the mechanics (Now the game will guide you through the gameplay);
[*] Addition of six Steam achievements;
[*] Improved graphics;
[*] Better compatibility with Remote Play;
[*] Daily maintenance;
[*] GENERAL maintenance of systems;
[/list]

Hello Steam users! We just released a new update for the Help Me Now game! This update can be classified as a small update, but there have been significant changes in the gameplay question! Check out the changes that this update brought:

[list]
[*] EXTRA optimization of very heavy areas;
[*] EXTRA polishing of the entire game;
[*] Correction of small bugs and lags;
[*] Change in the mechanics of picking up letters and notes (Now you can close the note / letter by pressing the "TAB" key or the "CLOSE" button on the screen);
[*] Improvements in adapting to control;
[*] Configurations of possible compatibility with Raytracing (Not yet implemented, but we are already in the process of configuration and implementation);
[*] Improvements in the Enemy's artificial intelligence;
[*] And much more!
[/list]

These were the changes that occurred in this update!
